## Install

The Sentry SDK for Ruby comes as a gem that should be added to your `Gemfile`:

```ruby
gem "sentry-ruby"
```

After adding the gems, run the following to install the SDK:

```ruby
bundle install
```

## Configure SDK

To use Sentry Ruby all you need is your DSN. Like most Sentry libraries it will honor the `SENTRY_DSN` environment variable. You can find it on the project settings page under API Keys. You can either export it as environment variable or manually configure it with `Sentry.init`:

```ruby

require 'sentry-ruby'

Sentry.init do |config|
  config.dsn = 'https://999392f8e932f53073ef42ff736d062b@o4512192354254848.ingest.de.sentry.io/4512192362446928'

  # Add data like request headers and IP for users,
  # see https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/ruby/data-management/data-collected/ for more info
  config.send_default_pii = true
end
```

## Verify

This snippet contains a deliberate error and message sent to Sentry and can be used as a test to make sure that everything's working as expected.

```ruby

begin
  1 / 0
rescue ZeroDivisionError => exception
  Sentry.capture_exception(exception)
end

Sentry.capture_message("test message")
```
